Z||000004||Cooter||04-25-2000||08:39 PM||||When I was racing karts, I raced in a "gas" class. So I bought some model airplane fuel- a little castor oil, methanol and 40% nitromethane to mix with my premium unleaded pump gas. The large blue flame from the header gave it away, but damn it was fast!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||04-25-2000||09:52 PM||||Just be sure your fuel system is compatible. I've heard that Methanol can dissolve or corrode certain common materials that gasoline won't bother. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||04-26-2000||01:03 AM||||I have been interested in finding a way to mix like toulene with my gas to get a higher octane but I dont' know the ratios of mix to use.  And to my knowlegde noone else seems to know the proper ratio and what octane it will make when mixed.<P>If what this guy says is true then my guess is because it works like nitrous by having a hotter combustion temp forcing the pistons down faster and all that other good stuff.  thing that bothers me is using this mixture with the nitrous.  Combustion temps getting too hot and melting something?  Perhaps.  Try it out I guess but I wouldn't do it with nitrous the first time out unless you have the money to rebuild if a piston burns<P>Is it safe to run nitromethane fuel in my Fiero with my nitrous?  What about without my nitrous?  My injectors able to flow nitromethane without ill effects?  Where does one get nitromethane?  Cooter?  Also any ratios for that concotion you made with the nitro and plane fuel?<P>Perhaps someone will come along with the correct info or try it who doesnt' give a F&*K if the engine blows up.<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fret Naught||04-26-2000||01:34 AM||||I haven't had much experience with high tess fuels, My dad God rest his soul was a real master. built rods, raced at Daytona smartest guy I ever knew. Said that the problem with nitrous was that it was necessary to use teflon pistons to prevent burning a hole in the pistons stock pistons couldn't stand the heat. Might be the same problem with a Meth mix. My two cents worth||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||04-26-2000||04:20 AM||||High alcohol concentrations will oxidize the aluminum components of the stock fuel injection system and interfere with proper operation of the oxygen sensor.  <P>If you want to know how to make octane booster, just do a search of the forum.  Toluene is an excellent octane booster when added by itself to a tank of gas, but I would not add more than 48 oz/tank.<P><BR>Mike B.<BR>(ACS Certified Analytical Chemist - Retired)||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||04-26-2000||08:27 AM||||i'd stay away from METHANE! it's exponentialy more volitile than Methanol! hummm I'm gunna make a few calls to Robinson Racing in Cumming, Ga. when they open maybe they can give me a mix idea.. they race a Cup Lite Infinity that runs off Methanol... i'll let ya know.||||reg||1
Z||000010||cobra427||04-26-2000||01:25 PM||||Shaun and others,<BR>I have some fomulars given by Randy Agee with reguards to Toulene,Xylene,MTBE-Methyl-tertiary-butyl-ether,Methanol or Ethanol,Isopropyl Alcohol and Tertiary Butyl Alcohol if anyone is interested. It is a lenghty discription which is why ask.There were no nitro methane figures tho. Let me know.<P>cobra427||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||04-27-2000||11:05 AM||||HOW SWEET!!! well i got 4 gallons of Methanol yesterday cost me $10. Went straight home and poured some in the new Kart and WOW thats loud! (3 stage header... cost me $20) Then figured what the heck i'll put some in the lawn mower... I added about 1 cup full to the 3/4 full tank on my Honda 5HP self propeled bagger. I shook it for a sec and pulled the handle to start it and WOW! its a totaly different mower! Sounds lame but DAM! it went from a stock grassy POS to a LOUD grass munchin' crazy machine... I figured a $250 mower was cheaper then my car if it blew up... The guys at the shop just purchased a BIG scatter shield that they can strap over your cars engine bay, while on the Dyno. Hope i won't need it but we'll see. I'll add 1 gallon of Methanol to 5 gallons gas and stick with that. I'll be sure to post my findings...  It will be after the middle of next month.. waiting for my new 4:10 tranny and support bearings.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  TOO COOL! ||||reg||10
Z||000012||Shaun41178||04-27-2000||09:24 PM||||Where does one go about buying Methanol?  Where is it available at?<P>So you guys think it is bad to add nitromethane to my fuel?  What about if I don't use my nitrous?<P>Hey Cobra, you want to post those ratios to the forum here?  I am interested in knowing them.  Or just email them to me at Shaun41178@aol.com  I would appreciate it very much.  Thanks<P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000013||cobra427||04-27-2000||10:16 PM||||Shaun and others,<BR>This the formula for Toulene<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||cobra427||04-27-2000||11:19 PM||||Shaun and others,<BR>This is the formula for Toulene<BR>===============================<BR>R+M/2......114<BR>Cost.......$2.50/gal (1998 prices)<P>Mixtures with 92 Octane<BR>-----------------------<BR>10%....94.2 octane<BR>20%....96.4 octane<BR>30%....98.6 octane<BR>Notes:-Common ingrediant in octane boosters ia a can.12-16 ounces will only raise octane 2-3 points.i.e. from 92to92.3<P>Formula #2 Xylene<BR>=================<BR>R+M/2....117<BR>Cost.....$2.75/gal (1998 prices)<P>Mixtures with 92 octane<BR>-----------------------<BR>10%.....94.5 octane<BR>20%.....97.0 octane<BR>30%.....99.5 octane<BR>Notes:-Similar to Toulene. 12-16 ounces will only raise octane 2-3 points.i.e. 92-92.3 Usually mixed with toulene and advertised as "race formula".<P>Formula #3 MTBE (Methyl-tertiary-butyl-ether)<BR>===============<BR>R+M/2.....118<BR>Cost......$3.50/gal (1998 prices)<P>Mixtures with 92 octane<BR>-----------------------<BR>10%.....94.6 octane<BR>20%.....97.2 octane<BR>30%.....99.8 octane<BR>Notes:-Oxygenate. Very common in octane booster products. Has lower BTU content than toulene and xylene, but oxygenate effect makes the gasoline burn better and produce more energy.<P>Formula #4 Methanol or Ethanol<BR>==============================<BR>R+M/2.....101<BR>Cost......$0.60-$1.75 (1998 prices)<P>Mixtures with 92 Octane<BR>-----------------------<BR>10%.....94.3 octane (Methanol)<BR>10%.....94.7 octane (Ethanol)<BR>20%.....Not Reccommended<BR>Notes:-Methanol is wood alcohol. Ethanol is a grain alcohol and found in Gasohol in 10% ratios.Both alcohols are mildly corrosive and will eat gas tank linings,rubber and aluminum if used in excessive ratios.<P>Formula #5 Isopropyl Alcohol and Tertiaty Butyl Alcohol<BR>=========================================<BR>R+M/2.....101<BR>Cost......$0.60-$1.50/ gal (1998 prices)<P>Mixtures with 92 Octane<BR>-----------------------<BR>10%......94.5 octane<BR>20%......Not Recommended<BR>30%......Not Recommended<BR>Notes:-Similar to Methanol/Ethanol. Isopropyl Alcohol is simply rubbing alcohol.<P><BR>Ok, all this having been noted, this is the basic formula for one of the popular octane booster products:-<BR>To make eight(8) 16 ounce bottles(128 ozs.= 1 gal.)<BR>100 ounces of toulene for octane boost<BR>25 ounces of mineral spirits (cleaning agent)<BR>3 ounces of Transmission fluid(lubing agent)<BR>Diesel fuel or kerosene may be substituted for mineral spirits and light turbine oil can be substituted for transmission fluid.<BR>Color can be added with petroleum dyes.<P>Hope that you can decipher all this. This was given originally by Randy Agee in 1998.<P>cobra427 <P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||04-28-2000||08:13 AM||||I purchased it at the local speed shop. There are quite a few Methanol bracket racers in the local area. You can contact VP racing fuels, or Shell. Both make and usually stock this. another alternative is aviation fuel. but it's MUCH more expensive... Methane is ALL kinds of bad.. even off nitrous you can do bad things... i'll get the burn rates for the 4 different types of fuel and post em..  BRB<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||1FST2M6||04-28-2000||08:19 AM||||from briggs&stratton racing web page... BTUs per .oz of fuel and lb. of air. <P>Gasoline         1359    $1.42 per gallon<BR>Ethanol          1418    $2.00 (hard to get)<BR>Methanol         1524    $2.50 per gallon<BR>Nitromethane     3034    $48.00 per gallon NOT A TYPE ERROR!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||1
